<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Status-bar (small) icon for the reminder notifications.

  Android renders a notification's small icon from its ALPHA CHANNEL ONLY and
  tints it with the notification colour, so this must be a white-on-transparent
  silhouette. Without this file the Capacitor plugin falls back to
  `android.R.drawable.ic_dialog_info` (LocalNotificationManager.getDefaultSmallIcon),
  which is a fully-opaque multi-colour system asset. Flattened to alpha it is a
  featureless white blob, which is why the reminder never looked like ours.

  THE GLYPH IS THE BARBELL (v403, owner decision): the five rectangles of
  ICONS.dumbbell, path for path, as one white silhouette, and the SAME geometry
  as the web badge in `icons/badge-96.png` (scripts/build-notif-icons.js BADGE).
  One glyph on both platforms, so a reminder looks the same on the phone as it
  does in a desktop browser. Contract 72 holds this file to the glyph.

  This file has now been four different marks: the five bars, the CUT tile at
  v216, the V-and-slot, and the barbell. Each time it lagged, because it CANNOT
  follow on its own: it is a native resource, it changes only when someone
  edits this file and rebuilds.

  ALPHA-ONLY: the gaps between each outer and inner plate are empty canvas,
  not painted shapes, so they survive the tint; the shaft is its own mass and
  needs no evenOdd.

  INK BOX: the glyph scaled 0.95 about its centre (the group's pivot 12,12):
  x 2.025..21.975, y 6.3..17.7, inside the 2..22 safe area, which leaves the
  margin a status bar wants at its ~18px render size.

  ⚠️ BAKED INTO THE APK. Editing this changes nothing for anyone until a new APK
  is built AND installed; `git push` cannot deliver a native resource. Verify a
  build by DECOMPILING, never by checking that a file with this name exists —
  that check is what missed the launcher-icon bug for three releases. Run
  `aapt2 dump xmltree` against the built APK, passing this path with its file
  flag, and read the actual pathData.

  (The flag is described rather than written out because it starts with two
  hyphens, and two hyphens are illegal inside an XML comment. Writing it here
  literally is what failed this very build the first time — the same trap that
  briefly broke icon.svg with `-` `-bg` in its comment.)
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <group
        android:scaleX="0.95"
        android:scaleY="0.95"
        android:pivotX="12"
        android:pivotY="12">
        <path
